[[ ## reasoning ## ]]
The primary issue in the previous implementation was an incorrect normalization step and rounding logic. 
1. The logic `if (product[22])` was applied to the product of two 11-bit significands (which range from 1.0 to 1.999...). The product of two such numbers ranges from 1.0 to 3.999... . Therefore, the product always has a bit at index 21 (for values < 2) or index 22 (for values >= 2).
2. The previous logic for `final_exp` adjustment and rounding was inconsistent with IEEE 754. Specifically, the normalization should check if the product >= 2 (i.e., bit 22 is set). If bit 22 is set, shift right by 1 and increment the exponent. 
3. The previous rounding logic `round_up = guard && (round || sticky || round_mant[0])` is slightly off for ties-to-even. The correct condition for rounding up at the half-way point (guard=1, round=0, sticky=0) is when the LSB is 1. The general condition for round-to-nearest-even is `guard && (round || sticky || mantissa_lsb)`.
4. I have cleaned up the shift, exponent adjustment, and rounding to ensure alignment with standard IEEE 754 rules for normalized significands.

